<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Shame itself. A situational thought whose stage comes from the total weight of everyone who
    is still carrying something they saw. Guilt is a ledger of deeds and it fades; this is a
    ledger of people and it does not. Nothing here decays on a clock. The only thing that moves
    the number down is one of those people coming back.

    Psychopath is nullified here. Sociopath is not, because that trait belongs to another mod in
    the set and naming it here would be a config error for anybody running this one on its own.
    It is handled in code instead, where a full Sociopath only ever counts the handful of people
    who are real to them. Bloodlust is deliberately NOT nullified, unlike Guilt: enjoying violence
    has nothing to do with whether being seen falling apart is humiliating.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>SH_Shame</defName>
    <workerClass>Shame.ThoughtWorker_Shame</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <developmentalStageFilter>Adult</developmentalStageFilter>
    <nullifyingTraits>
      <li>Psychopath</li>
    </nullifyingTraits>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>they saw</label>
        <description>Somebody was standing right there. I keep going over what it must have looked like from where they were.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-3</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>I know what they think of me</label>
        <description>They have not said anything. They do not have to. I was there too, and I know what I looked like.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-7</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>I am what they saw</label>
        <description>It was not a bad day. A bad day is a thing that happens to you. That was me, and enough people watched it that there is no arguing with it now.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-12</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!--
    Pointed at one particular person: the shamed colonist cannot be around somebody who was
    there. The opinion drops on THEIR side, not the witness's - the witness may think nothing
    of it at all. That asymmetry is the whole mod. Shame pushes a colonist away from exactly
    the people who could end it.

    Staged by how much that one witness is carrying, so somebody who saw one bad evening is not
    the same as somebody who has watched them come apart four times.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>SH_TheySawMe</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Shame.Thought_Witnessed</thoughtClass>
    <workerClass>Shame.ThoughtWorker_TheySawMe</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <developmentalStageFilter>Adult</developmentalStageFilter>
    <nullifyingTraits>
      <li>Psychopath</li>
    </nullifyingTraits>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>they were there</label>
        <baseOpinionOffset>-6</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>they have seen me like that</label>
        <baseOpinionOffset>-13</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>they know exactly what I am</label>
        <baseOpinionOffset>-22</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!--
    The other end of it. A witness who kept coming back until there was nothing left to carry.

    This is the only thing in the mod that heals anything, and it is worth more than the shame
    it replaced: being seen at your worst by somebody who then turned out to still want your
    company is a stronger tie than never having been seen at all.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>SH_TheyStayed</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Thought_MemorySocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>45</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>200</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>2</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stackedEffectMultiplier>0.75</stackedEffectMultiplier>
    <nullifyingTraits>
      <li>Psychopath</li>
    </nullifyingTraits>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>they stayed</label>
        <baseOpinionOffset>18</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
